<title>FINLAND: YIT SHAREHOLDERS APPROVE REDEMPTION CLAUSE.</title>
<headline>YIT SHAREHOLDERS APPROVE REDEMPTION CLAUSE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish construction group YIT-Yhtyma Oy said in a statement on Monday its extraordinary shareholders meeting had included a share redemption clause in the company's bylaws.</p>
<p>&quot;According to the decision, a shareholder with more than a third and/or more than half of shares ... has to make an offer to redeem the rest of the outstanding shares,&quot; YIT said.</p>
<p>The board's proposal for the clause was announced on October 14.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 242</p>
